From e1c840bf90e4138735db86b73c48c6d9ed4d0d73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add screenshot import: scan a bank-app ledger screenshot with
 AI

Users can upload up to 5 screenshots of their bank app's transaction
list. A vision model reads them via a new extract_transactions action on
the ai-assist edge function; the user reviews and edits every row before
anything is written to the ledger.

- Edge function: vision call (GROQ_VISION_MODEL, default qwen/qwen3.8-27b),
  strict server-side sanitizing of model output (dates, amounts, type,
  category ids, row cap), prompt-injection-safe prompt
- Client: browser-side image compression, one-for-one duplicate detection
  against the ledger and earlier screenshots, editable review screen with
  per-row select, date/type/category/amount edits
- Rows without a readable date or flagged as duplicates start unchecked
- EN/FR/AR translations, new "Scan a screenshot" entry in the data menu

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ArFS2qniZYkZrVFsQ3UH1P
